  set:  # 767b
    description: "**Symptom:** Updating any tracker item with a description (or other long string field) whose UTF-8 byte length plus YAML overhead exceeds ~4096 bytes causes the per-line nonce comment to be embedded literally INSIDE the string value on read-back. The corrupted text appears as `  # <nonce>` between adjacent words at the YAML fold boundary. Bug fires deterministically.\n\n**Root cause** (verified 2026-04-08 by reading store.py at HEAD):\n1. `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/store.py:289` sets `ry.width = 4096`. ruamel.yaml folds long double-quoted scalars across physical lines (newline + leading whitespace, read back as a single space).\n2. `store.py:298-303` post-processes the dumped YAML by appending `  # <nonce>` to EVERY non-empty physical line, INCLUDING multi-line scalar continuation lines.\n3. CSafeLoader (`store.py:316-333`) treats `#` as literal inside double-quoted scalars, so the appended nonce comment becomes part of the string value.\n\n**Reproduction:** create or update an item with a description over ~4080 UTF-8 bytes. See INV-gajap discussion for the original observation; this item's own first-revision description (4708 bytes, filed via the same bug) contained THREE real nonce injections — see discussion below for the corruption trace.\n\n**Workaround:** keep description strings under ~4080 UTF-8 bytes. Push detail beyond that into discussion entries (separate scalars, no fold).\n\n**Proposed fixes** (in order of preference): see discussion entry \"Proposed fixes\" below.\n\n**Tests to add:** see discussion entry \"Tests to add\" below.\n\n**Why structural, not cosmetic:** see discussion entry \"Why structural\" below."  # 767b
