  message: "[Discovery context] Discovered while updating INV-gajap to correct stale 'on_transcript_change.py' file paths to '.agent/hooks/_shared/on_transcript_change.py'. The fields.root_cause update (a short field) landed cleanly; the description update (long field, 4106 YAML bytes) corrupted at position 'periodic  # f084 audit'. A second attempt with restructured paragraph corrupted at position 'Validation  # 418f cadence:' — same bug, new wrap point. INV-gajap description was ultimately reverted to its pre-update text and the path correction recorded in a discussion entry instead. Then this very item was filed via the same bug — its own first-revision description (4708 bytes) self-corrupted at three positions, this time read back as: literal '# f084 nonce should not...' near 'serializer fix; until then', literal '# 418f' embedded somewhere in the proposed-fixes paragraph, and literal '# dc1a' embedded in the regression-tests paragraph. (The literal '# abcd' in the original test-fixture sentence was intentional and is NOT a corruption hit.) After this restructure, the description sits below the ~4080-byte threshold and the verbose detail lives in these discussion entries (which are stored as separate scalars and do not fold)."  # 847b
- op: discuss  # fe0a
  at: '2026-04-08T23:18:15Z'  # fe0a
  by: agent  # fe0a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fe0a
  clock: 7  # fe0a
  nonce: fe0a  # fe0a
  message: "[Proposed fixes — revised 2026-04-08 after reviewer discussion] Supersedes the earlier [Proposed fixes] entry above for purposes of implementation. Two changes from the original list: (A) DROP option 3 (raise ry.width to 1_000_000). Reviewer noted that while .ops files are append-only and the per-line nonce design (ADR-0013) makes line-based merge robustness non-load-bearing on width, raising width to 1M produces visually coarse single-line scalars in `git diff` and `gh pr diff` output for any large description. Prefer keeping width modest and fixing the post-processor instead. A small safety bump (e.g. width=8192) is fine as defense in depth, but is optional. (B) ADD a new fix proposal targeting the auto-sync notification stream: currently the line `[tracker] Auto-sync is AUTOMATIC...` is printed to STDOUT for all commands, including read-only ones, which pollutes machine-readable output and forces callers to discover --no-auto-sync. Proposed: when --json is set, route the notification to stderr instead of stdout. When --json is NOT set, keep current stdout behavior so naive shell users see the warning prominently and don't fall into the manual-sync footgun. Optional belt-and-braces: when pending lines exceed 2x threshold, the next mutation exits non-zero unless an explicit --allow-pending-overflow flag is passed — exit code is universal across all agent harnesses regardless of whether they read stderr. Final recommended fix set: option 1 (skip continuation lines in the post-processor at store.py:298-303) + the new --json-aware notification routing + optionally option 3' (modest width bump to 8192 as safety margin) + optionally the 2x-threshold hard-stop. The combination eliminates the corruption AND removes the JSON-pollution paper cut AND structurally prevents manual-sync mistakes."  # fe0a
